<body>
	<dt>peace</dt>
	<dd>
		the active, unshakeable stillness that absorbs external chaos without reacting to it. the ultimate, quiet exertion of personal control.
	</dd>
	<dt>harmony: the drive to find, create, and maintain underlying balance. tuning the noise of the world into a resonant, functional system.
		</li>
		<li>
			discernment: the sharp, clear-eyed ability to see through manipulation and read the true dynamics of a situation, person, or system.
		</li>
		<li>
			self-reliance: the quiet confidence of knowing you have the tools, the stamina, and the inner sanctuary to sustain yourself independently.
		</li>
		<li>
			boundaries: the deliberate protection of your mental energy and time from external demands that do not serve your core structure.
		</li>
		<li>
			objective resilience: the capacity to remain grounded when things break, assessing root causes and fixing them without absorbing the surrounding panic.
		</li>
		<li>
			analytical depth: the relentless curiosity to look past the surface of a task or problem to understand the absolute bedrock infrastructure beneath it.
		</li>
		<li>
			intellectual thoroughness: the commitment to meticulous, deliberate exploration. doing the deep work to truly master a system, a narrative, or a craft.
		</li>
		<li>
			energy conservation: the intentional refusal of false urgency. saving your bandwidth for what actually matters rather than burning out on forced external output.
		</li>
		<li>
			pacing: moving at your own natural, deliberate speed. treating life and creation as a long-term build rather than a frantic sprint.
		</li>
		<li>
			generosity: extending grace, resources, and shared knowledge to yourself and others, completely free from the anxiety of scarcity.
		</li>
		<li>
			abundance mindset: the belief that there is enough time, comfort, and joy available in the present moment to build a good life right now.
		</li>
		<li>
			raw honesty: the uncompromising commitment to structural truth over comfort, seeking authentic connection and stripping away pretenses.
		</li>
		<li>
			aesthetics: the tactile and visual pursuit of beauty. the satisfaction of making something not just functional, but elegantly designed and pleasing to experience.
		</li>
		<li>
			passion: the deep, internal fuel that drives you to create, connect, and build meaning on your own uncompromising terms.
		</li>
	</ul>

